spans.s:
khaḍga,
(1) nt., a high number (cf. khaḍgin): Mmk 〔262.15〕 adhikā daśa tare (?) tasya (sc. vivāhasya, cf. line 14) khaḍgam ity āhu vāṇijāḥ; 〔343.14〕 daśārbudā nirbudaḥ uktaḥ taddaśaṃ khaḍgam iṣyate;
(2) m., n. of a mountain: Māy 〔254.6〕.

khaḍgin,
(1) m., or khaḍgina, nt. (cf. khaḍga), a high number: Mmk 〔262.16〕 (vs) nikhaḍgaṃ (q.v.) tad vidur mantrī nikhaḍgaṃ cāpi khaḍginam (follows line 15 cited s.v. khaḍga, and seems to mean that khaḍga, nikhaḍga, and khaḍgin(a) are interchangeable terms);
(2) m., a Pratyekabuddha (because he is often compared to a rhinoceros, Skt. khaḍgin; see s.v. khaḍgaviṣāṇa): Mmk 〔67.9, 14〕; 〔122.7〕; 〔156.7〕; 〔238.5〕; also pratyeka-khaḍgin, 〔108.23〕; 〔112.20〕; 〔114.21〕; 〔169.26〕.
